title: Global shell › Sidebar › Authorizations group › Open and close the group
route: Every page (sidebar, the 'Authorizations' row)
intro: The 'Authorizations' row has two parts. The label and the rest of the row are a link to /authorizations. The arrow at its right is its own button: it shows or hides the three sub rows without leaving the page. The group opens by itself when the address enters an Authorizations page, and otherwise keeps the person's choice.
dir: TD
also: The open or closed choice lives in the page, not in the demo data: 'Reset demo data' keeps it. A browser reload starts again: open when the page is an Authorizations page, closed anywhere else. Authorizations pages are /authorizations (every view), a case page, New Case and Eligibility & Benefits.
---
start s1 "Psyflo opens on a page"
decision d0 "Is it an Authorizations page?"
process o0 "Group open\nSub rows 'All Authorizations', 'New Case' 4, 'Eligibility & Benefits' 9\nArrow points down"
process c0 "Group closed\nOnly the 'Authorizations' row, badge 19\nArrow points right"
screen row "'Authorizations' row\nIcon, label, badge, then the arrow"
decision d1 "Which part does the person use?"

group gArrow "The arrow button"
  click a1 "Click the arrow\nTooltip 'Expand' or 'Collapse'"
  click aK "Tab to the arrow and press Enter or Space\nScreen readers hear 'Expand Authorizations' or 'Collapse Authorizations', and whether it is expanded"
  decision d2 "Is the group open?"
  process a2 "The three sub rows hide\nArrow points right"
  process a3 "The three sub rows show under 'Authorizations'\nArrow points down"
  process a4 "The address does not change and the page stays exactly as it was\nFrom the Dashboard, for example, the group opens in place and 'Dashboard' stays green"
endgroup

group gLabel "The label link"
  click l1 "Click 'Authorizations'\n(the label, the icon, the badge or any empty part of the row)"
  process l2 "Go to /authorizations"
  goto gW "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Arrive and read the views"
endgroup

process p0 "The address changes"
start s2 "Any other link, sidebar row, redirect or the Back button changes the address"
decision d3 "Did the address just come into an Authorizations page from another page?"
process u1 "The group opens by itself\neven if the person closed it before leaving"
process u2 "The group keeps the person's choice\nClosed stays closed while moving between Authorizations pages\nOpen stays open after leaving for another page"

decision d4 "Is the group closed while an Authorizations page is open?"
process h1 "The whole 'Authorizations' row, arrow included, is the green row\nThe place is never lost while the sub rows are hidden"
process h2 "The green row is a sub row ('All Authorizations', 'New Case', 'Eligibility & Benefits') or a row outside the group"
goto gHi "Continues in: Global shell › Sidebar › Which row is green"
end e1 "Sidebar shows the group the way the person left it"

s1 --> d0
d0 -->|Yes| o0 --> row
d0 -->|No| c0 --> row
row --> d1
d1 -->|The arrow| a1 --> d2
d1 -->|Keyboard| aK --> d2
d2 -->|Open| a2 --> a4
d2 -->|Closed| a3 --> a4
d1 -->|The label| l1 --> l2 --> p0
l2 --> gW
s2 --> p0 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| u1 --> d4
d3 -->|No| u2 --> d4
a4 --> d4
d4 -->|Yes| h1 --> e1
d4 -->|No| h2 --> e1
h2 -.-> gHi
